course: dictionary
lesson: 10168
title: A tic is a habit you cannot help
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A tic is a sudden movement or sound that a person makes again and again without meaning to. Blinking, shrugging, sniffing and clearing the throat are all tics. Tic is a noun, so it names a thing.
explain: Context helps you spot a tic. Something done without meaning to comes with clues like sudden or again and again. In «Long words are read in chunks called syllables», the last chunk of fan-tas-tic is also tic, but that is just a sound in a word, not a movement a person makes.
explain: Some tics are in how a person talks. A verbal tic is a habit word, like always saying «like». It is a tic in words, not in the body.
explain: People with tics cannot simply stop, so never tease them or copy them.
fact: A tic is a sudden movement or sound that happens again and again without meaning to.
fact: Common tics include blinking, shrugging, sniffing and clearing the throat.
fact: A verbal tic is a habit in how someone talks, like always saying «like».
fact: Tics are common in childhood and often come and go.
fact: Tics can be part of Tourette's syndrome, and people with tics cannot just stop, so never tease or copy them.
exercise: A tic is a sudden movement or sound that a person makes again and again without meaning to. What is a tic? | A planned dance step | A long word cut into chunks | A kind of cake | *A sudden movement or sound made again and again without meaning to
exercise: Ella says a verbal tic is a kind of dance. What is a verbal tic? | *A habit word, like always saying «like» | A page in a book | A loud shout at a football match | A kind of fish
exercise: Which of these is a tic? | Cooking dinner | Painting a picture | Reading a book on purpose | *Blinking again and again without meaning to
test: In «Long words are read in chunks called syllables», what is the last chunk of fan-tas-tic? | *tic | sand | pic | fan
test: Why should you never tease someone who has tics? | Because tics make them grow | Because tics are a kind of game | *Because they cannot simply stop | Because tics are fun to copy
exam: Which best describes a tic? | *Sudden movements or sounds made again and again without meaning to | A kind of pudding | Planned moves in a game | Long words in books
